        <headline>Small Craft Advisory issued September 26 at 2:51PM EDT until September 27 at 6:00PM EDT by NWS Baltimore MD/Washington DC</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...For the Gale Warning, north winds 15 to 20 kt with gusts
up to 35 kt. For the Small Craft Advisory, northwest winds 10 to
20 kt with gusts up to 30 kt expected.

* WHERE...Chesapeake Bay north of Pooles Island MD and Choptank
River to Cambridge MD and the Little Choptank River.

* WHEN...For the Gale Warning, until 10 PM EDT this evening. For
the Small Craft Advisory, from 10 PM this evening to 6 PM EDT
Sunday.

* IMPACTS...Strong winds will cause hazardous waves which could
capsize or damage vessels.
</description>
        <instruction>Mariners should alter plans to avoid these hazardous conditions.
Remain in port, seek safe harbor, alter course, and/or secure the
vessel for hazardous conditions.</instruction>
